s ago, we can use the modulo operation to find the remainder when 200 is divided by 7. This will tell us how many days before a full number of weeks we need to count.\n\n1. Perform the division \\(200 \\div 7\\):\n   \\[\n   200 \\div 7 = 28 \\text{ R } 4\n   \\]\n   This means that 200 days is equivalent to 28 weeks and 4 extra days. Since 28 weeks is a whole number of weeks, it brings us back to the same day of the week. Therefore, we only need to count back 4 days from Wednesday.\n\n2. Counting back 4 days from Wednesday:\n   - 1 day before Wednesday is Tuesday,\n   - 2 days before Wednesday is Monday,\n   - 3 days before Wednesday is Sunday,\n   - 4 days before Wednesday is Saturday.\n\nTherefore, 200 days ago was a Saturday. The day of the week Kim's birthday fell on is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
